        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T15:56:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me keep this behavior because:\n  - In case that `pvmfw` has more version in the future, then we can\u0027t decide which version to pick.\n  - it allows `null`, so bump up also mean bump down. It may",
      "parentUuid": "72b785fd_d6c23811",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 203,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d9c87d94b1aeccda15c8064b676044cf91aee0df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "705813f6_e8f33821",
        "filename": "tests/pvmfw/helper/java/com/android/pvmfw/test/host/Pvmfw.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 203,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T16:27:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking if you call setFoo, where foo requires version x, then we set the version to max(x, whatever it was before).\n\nDo you really want set(null) to be valid?\n\nNot a big deal, tbf.",
      "parentUuid": "9fefe1f8_32861241",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 203,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d9c87d94b1aeccda15c8064b676044cf91aee0df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
